<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Modernism</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Modernism was an artistic and cultural movement of the late nineteenth and early twentieth centuries that broke with traditional forms. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a>'s profile, the Benin bronzes looted in 1897 influenced European modernism through the admiration of artists such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso">Picasso</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-matisse">Matisse</a>. African art more broadly was an important source for modernist artists.</p></div>
